**Common Web Element Mistakes and Solutions:**

**1. Not Waiting for Elements**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
driver.get("https://example.com");
driver.findElement(By.id("dynamicElement")).click();
// Fails with NoSuchElementException
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement element = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id("dynamicElement"))
);
element.click();
```

**2. Using getText() for Input Fields**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
WebElement input = driver.findElement(By.id("username"));
input.sendKeys("testuser");
String value = input.getText(); // Returns empty string!
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
String value = input.getAttribute("value"); // Returns "testuser"
```

**3. Not Checking Element State Before Interaction**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
WebElement button = driver.findElement(By.id("submit"));
button.click(); // May fail if button is disabled or hidden
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
if (button.isDisplayed() && button.isEnabled()) {
    button.click();
} else {
    System.out.println("Button not ready for interaction");
}
```

**4. Stale Element References**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("item"));
driver.navigate().refresh(); // Page refreshed
element.click(); // Throws StaleElementReferenceException
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// Re-find element after page change
WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("item"));
driver.navigate().refresh();
element = driver.findElement(By.id("item")); // Find again
element.click();
```

**5. Not Clearing Input Before Typing**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
WebElement field = driver.findElement(By.id("search"));
// Field already contains "old text"
field.sendKeys("new text"); // Results in "old textnew text"
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
field.clear();
field.sendKeys("new text"); // Results in "new text"
```

**6. Incorrect Checkbox/Radio Toggling**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Always clicking without checking state
checkbox.click(); // May unselect if already selected
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
if (!checkbox.isSelected()) {
    checkbox.click(); // Only click if not selected
}
```

**7. Ignoring ElementNotInteractableException**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
driver.findElement(By.id("button")).click();
// Element exists but is covered by overlay
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// Wait for overlay to disappear first
wait.until(ExpectedConditions.invisibilityOfElementLocated(By.id("overlay")));
wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id("button"))).click();
```

**8. Using Wrong Locator Strategy**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Fragile XPath
driver.findElement(By.xpath("/html/body/div[1]/div[2]/form/input[3]"));
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// More reliable locators
driver.findElement(By.id("username"));
driver.findElement(By.name("username"));
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("input[name='username']"));
```

**9. Not Handling Multiple Elements**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Only gets first element
WebElement item = driver.findElement(By.className("item"));
// Ignores other matching elements
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// Get all matching elements
List<WebElement> items = driver.findElements(By.className("item"));
for (WebElement item : items) {
    System.out.println(item.getText());
}
```

**10. Forgetting Import Statements**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Missing imports causes compilation errors
Select dropdown = new Select(element); // Cannot find symbol
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.WebDriverWait;
