```

**11. Not Scrolling to Element**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Element below fold, not in viewport
element.click(); // May fail
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;
js.executeScript("arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);", element);
element.click();
```

**12. Hardcoding Waits with Thread.sleep()**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
Thread.sleep(5000); // Always waits 5 seconds
driver.findElement(By.id("element")).click();
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id("element"))).click();
// Waits only as long as needed, up to 10 seconds
```

**Best Practices Summary:**

1. Always use explicit waits for dynamic elements
2. Verify element state (isDisplayed, isEnabled) before interaction
3. Use getAttribute("value") for input fields, not getText()
4. Clear input fields before typing new text
5. Re-find elements after page changes to avoid stale references
6. Check selection state before toggling checkboxes
7. Wait for overlays to disappear before clicking
8. Use reliable locator strategies (id, name, css)
9. Handle collections with findElements() when needed
10. Scroll to elements if they're below the fold

